; Provetrail event envelope, v0.1 (SPEC.md Section 8).
;
; CDDL cannot express encoding-level rules, so this schema is necessarily the
; weaker half of the contract: the deterministic-encoding profile (definite
; lengths only, shortest heads, bytewise-sorted keys on their encoded form) and
; the canonical re-derivation check are normative in SPEC.md and are what the
; invalid vectors exercise. A structure valid here can still be rejected there.

; Member notes:
;   actor          - the closed producer category; anything else is rejected
;                    (enc.invalid_actor).
;   seq            - int64, >= 1 (bound normative in SPEC.md), strictly
;                    increasing within a stream, gaps permitted.
;   time           - Unix nanoseconds UTC, int64. Advisory; ordering is by seq.
event = {
  actor: "agent" / "human" / "system",
  ? causation_id: tstr,
  ? origin_instance_id: tstr,
  payload: { * tstr => payload-value },
  ? principal: tstr,
  schema_version: int,
  seq: uint,
  ? span_id: tstr,
  stream: tstr,
  "time": int,
  ? trace_id: tstr,
  type: tstr,
}

; The payload value model: the I-JSON-compatible subset plus byte strings.
; Floating-point values and CBOR tags are prohibited at this version.
payload-value = tstr
              / bstr
              / int
              / bool
              / nil
              / [ * payload-value ]
              / { * tstr => payload-value }
